# Working-tree contract for a repo developed on Windows, built on macOS, and
# run on Linux -- handbook engineering/local_development.md, Layer 5.
#
# ONE COPY: this file (ci-scripts templates/gitattributes) is the source; each
# repo carries a copy and may ADD lines below it. The org gate (repo-lint)
# checks for the `* text=auto eol=lf` line, not for byte equality
# (narthelix/ops#2308).
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) writes CRLF into
# deploy/*.sh, and a script committed that way dies on the cluster with
# `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` -- a failure that is invisible on the
# machine that caused it. The enforcement is this file, deliberately, not a
# per-developer core.autocrlf setting nobody can verify.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Executed by a Linux shell or parsed by Linux tooling -- never CRLF, even if
# content sniffing were to guess otherwise.
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF, for the day one lands here.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.webp     binary
*.ico      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.zip      binary
*.jks      binary
*.keystore binary
*.p12      binary
*.jar      binary
*.apk      binary
*.aab      binary
*.mp3      binary
*.ogg      binary
*.wav      binary
*.mp4      binary
*.mov      binary
*.webm     binary
